    <abstract>This study is based on the Grassworks data (Temperton et al. 2025, https://doi.org/10.1111/rec.70109). Location: Mesic hay meadows and semi-dry calcareous grasslands in three ecoregions in northern, central, and southern Germany. Methods: In total, 621 vegetation surveys were conducted at restored sites (401) as well as positive (102) and negative references (118). All vegetation surveys were assigned to EUNIS habitat types. Community-weighted means (CWM) were calculated for specific leaf area (SLA), canopy height, and seed mass with trait values from the GIFT database</abstract>
